s humidly held together by what is  scientifically known as glowy purple  stuff  it's a light machine gun designed for  crowd control its huge clip  rapid fire rate and exceptionally high  stability and accuracy  as well as the ability to slow down  enemies and trigger singularity  explosions almost make up for the fact  that it's made up from a bunch of gross  alien  bones if heavy metal was a weapon it'd  be the amber vault  which smushes together bones amber cloth  chains and what looks like someone's  scalp and somehow ends up as an  incredible double gun  if that wasn't already metal enough this  enemy mulching firearms abilities are  called killing spree  and brain eater finally we have  voodoo matchmaker a red-hot assault  rifle that is literally  always on fire it's decked out in  various charms and trinkets  and of course bones always bones  we assume these adornments are what give  it the ability to sap life from up to  three  enemies simultaneously and make them  vulnerable to increased  damage now weapons alone not even  legendary ones will guarantee survival  against the relentless hordes of  insurgents and  other altered on enoch  when selecting your class it's useful to  know what powers they will ultimately  have at their disposal  each of the four classes trickster  pyromancer devastator and technomancer  can unlock eight powers in total  four of which can be assigned at any  time understanding how these powers  combine with each other as well as your  fellow outriders powers will be critical  in building an  enemy slaughtering powerhouse tricksters  specialise in close range get in get out  combat  with powers designed to disorientate and  pick apart enemies  the sweeping temporal slice strikes  multiple enemies  paralyzing anything unfortunate enough  to be caught in its wake  it's perfect for controlling larger  groups or simply for lining up headshots  on single enemies  speaking of crowd control the slow trap  power summons a dome that slows down  both enemies and projectiles in its  radius  it's an incredibly versatile ability  that will give your entire squad time to  weave between bullets  and dodge melee attacks while they turn  everything to mincemeat  it's also the perfect way to buy time if  you need to revive  a downed teammate these two abilities  work well in tandem too  slow your enemies down to a crawl with  slow trap and add salt to the wound with  temporal slice  to give your long range favoring  accomplices some easy target  practice and when we think of long range  we think of technomancers as well as  boasting passive long-range weapon  damage buffs  these support specialists are perfect  for self and group healing  as well as introducing additional  sources of damage and status effects to  the battlefield  tool of destruction gives you the choice  of summoning a minigun or rocket  launcher which is a bit like trying to  pick between your two favorite ice cream  flavors  your choice should really reflect your  circumstances the minigun offers raw  dps advantage tearing through enoch's  hostile population with satisfying ease  but when you're up against tougher  enemies like captains and bosses  the rpg's ability to interrupt their  ruinous charged attacks is essential for  survival  we're also fans of the appropriately  named pain launcher  here the technomancer materializes an  automated missile launcher  that fires off a volley of explosive  devastation over a steadily  increasing arc and offers another means  of interrupting  big attacks if you prefer your mances a  little more hot and steamy  then the pyromancer's predilection for  burning everything to the ground  should get you fired up as you'd expect  from a flame wielding outrider the  pyromancer  is big on area of effect powers and so  is best suited to mid-range combat  their thermal bomb lets you interrupt an  unfortunate recipient  and leave them with a nasty burn  chipping away at their health over time  if said status effect ends up completely  depleting their energy  they'll become a bomb themselves and  damage any other enemies in their blast  radius  ash blast which is quite hard to say  without sounding a bit like sean connery  works well with thermal bomb  because it completely immobilizes  enemies within its radius  if one of them is also afflicted with  burn it makes it far  easier to blast away the remnants of  their health to trigger an explosion  finally there's the devastator who  despite their name  is quite the softy now just kidding  they're absolute beasts who service your  squad's tank  able to buff their hp and armor beyond  any other class  and equipped with powers designed to  keep them firmly in the heart of battle  gravity leap perfectly illustrates this  with the devastator transforming into a  collection of hovering rocks  and then reforming as they crash back  down on an enemy  not only is it likely to turn grunts  into a cloud of red  it'll also deal aoe damage to anything  else in the vicinity  gravity leap is the perfect way to  follow up after triggering endless mass  which turns an enemy into a floating  obelisk with its own gravitational pull  do not question the science it is simply  very cool  its ability to group enemies makes it  very useful for subsequent  aoe attacks and that is just a fraction  of the savage powers and legendarily  lethal weapons  that will help you unleash hell on enoch  when the creative co-op chaos of  outriders launches  april 1st  [Music]

